---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import PageBody from "../components/PageBody.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import TokenTable from "../components/api/TokenTable.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "anatomy", label: "Anatomy", heading: false },
  { id: "styles", label: "Styles" },
  { id: "custom", label: "Color, width and speed" },
  { id: "accessibility", label: "Accessibility" },
  { id: "tokens", label: "Tokens" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="aura">
<PageBody sections={S}>
  <Section {...S.anatomy}>
        <p class="flow-text">
          An <code>.aura</code> wraps one element and runs a light around its
          border. Use it on the button, card or panel a screen most needs the
          user to notice, such as the plan you recommend or the action that
          finishes a setup.
        </p>
        <p>
          Keep it to one aura per screen. Two lights compete, and the effect
          stops pointing anywhere. The ring is 2px and sits just outside the
          wrapped element. Reduced motion stops the turning and keeps the ring.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap align-center gap-6 mb-3">
          <div class="aura"><button class="filled">Upgrade</button></div>
          <div class="aura">
            <article style="max-width: 18rem;">
              <h3>Pro plan</h3>
              <p>Unlimited projects and priority support.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="aura">
  <button class="filled">Upgrade</button>
</div>

<div class="aura">
  <article>
    <h3>Pro plan</h3>
    <p>Unlimited projects and priority support.</p>
  </article>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.styles}>
        <p>
          <code>dual</code> sends two lights around the ring, primary and
          tertiary, on opposite sides. <code>rainbow</code> turns the whole hue
          wheel. <code>glow</code> draws a blurred halo behind the element in
          place of a ring, so give the element an opaque container, such as a
          filled button or a card.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap align-center gap-6 mb-3">
          <div class="aura dual"><button class="tonal">Dual</button></div>
          <div class="aura rainbow"><button class="outlined">Rainbow</button></div>
          <div class="aura glow"><button class="filled">Glow</button></div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="aura dual"><button class="tonal">Dual</button></div>
<div class="aura rainbow"><button class="outlined">Rainbow</button></div>
<div class="aura glow"><button class="filled">Glow</button></div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.custom}>
        <p>
          Set the tokens on the <code>.aura</code>. The ring takes its corners
          from <code>--md-comp-aura-shape</code>: 12px to match a card, and
          fully rounded when it wraps a button. Set it to the corner size of
          anything else you wrap.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap align-center gap-6 mb-3">
          <div class="aura" style="--md-comp-aura-color: var(--md-sys-color-tertiary); --md-comp-aura-width: 4px; --md-comp-aura-duration: 2s;">
            <article style="max-width: 18rem;">
              <h3>Faster and wider</h3>
              <p>A 4px tertiary ring that turns every two seconds.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="aura" style="--md-comp-aura-color: var(--md-sys-color-tertiary);
                         --md-comp-aura-width: 4px;
                         --md-comp-aura-duration: 2s">
  <article>…</article>
</div>
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.accessibility}>
        <p>
          The light is decoration. It is drawn by a pseudo-element, so the
          wrapper adds nothing to the accessibility tree and the wrapped
          element keeps its own name and role. Do not rely on the aura to say
          that something is recommended; put that in the text, for example a
          "Recommended" badge or heading. In forced colors the ring is a solid
          <code>Highlight</code> outline.
        </p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.tokens}>
        <p>Override these on the <code>.aura</code>, or on a parent.</p>
        <TokenTable>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-aura-color</code></td>
            <td><code>--md-sys-color-primary</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-aura-color-2</code></td>
            <td><code>--md-sys-color-tertiary</code>; used by <code>dual</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-aura-width</code></td>
            <td>2px</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-aura-shape</code></td>
            <td>12px; 9999px around a button</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>--md-comp-aura-duration</code></td>
            <td>4s</td>
          </tr>
        </TokenTable>
  </Section>
</PageBody>
</DocsLayout>
